      <div type="work" n="178">
        <pb n="225"/>
        <head>Another : and it was composed because of the monasteries round the church, which were rejoicing at the commemoration of martyrs.</head>
        <head>178 — xiv — VI. — <quote>Let this be written for the succeeding generation</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="1">The bravery<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/> of the holy martyrs is a portrait<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/> of excellence, and a prefiguration of the chaste life [of abstinence and industry<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/>. If then we duly celebrate their memories, we<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/> shall delineate on [our person<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a6" target="#n6" n="6"/> their combat and their contests, by [living in<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a7" target="#n7" n="7"/> chastity and<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a8" target="#n8" n="8"/> practising asceticism, and<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a9" target="#n9" n="9"/> displaying all labour in good things, [in order<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a10" target="#n10" n="10"/> that we may not miss and fall <pb n="226"/> short of [imitating their excellence. Thus<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a11" target="#n11" n="11"/> <persName>Paul</persName> also in a certain place admonished, saying, <quote>Observing<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a12" target="#n12" n="12"/> the end of the conversation and of the conduct in life of those men, imitate<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a13" target="#n13" n="13"/> their faith</quote>. For they who devote themselves to the [love of pleasure<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a14" target="#n14" n="14"/> and honour the champions (<foreign xml:lang="grc">ἀγωνισταί</foreign>)<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a15" target="#n15" n="15"/> with the lips only do not know that they are only deceiving and making a mockery of themselves. Wherefore we beg<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a16" target="#n16" n="16"/> thee, Lord, through<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a17" target="#n17" n="17"/> their entreaties allow and grant us [to serve and to keep thy<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a18" target="#n18" n="18"/> commandments, and the riches of thy great mercy.</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 225, n. 2</orig></choice> Ps. cii, 19.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 225, n. 3</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>combat</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 225, n. 4</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>draughtsman's tablet, a picture</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 225, n. 5</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>ascetic and industrious</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 225, n. 6</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>of these, we</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 225, n. 7</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>ourselves</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n7" target="#a7" n="7"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 225, n. 8</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>practising</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n8" target="#a8" n="8"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 225, n. 9</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>by</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n9" target="#a9" n="9"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 225, n. 9</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>by</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n10" target="#a10" n="10"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 225, n. 10</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>to (the end)</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n11" target="#a11" n="11"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 226, n. 1</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>imitating them. This</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n12" target="#a12" n="12"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 226, n. 2</orig></choice> Heb. xiii, 7, 8 <quote>Remember..... <persName>Jesus Christ</persName> is yesterday and to-day and, for ever</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n13" target="#a13" n="13"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 226, n. 3</orig></choice> Id. vi, 11, 12 (cited as Philem.).</note>
        <note xml:id="n14" target="#a14" n="14"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 226, n. 4</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>pleasure of passions</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n15" target="#a15" n="15"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 226, n. 5</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>combatants</quote> (<foreign xml:lang="grc">ἀθληταί</foreign>).</note>
        <note xml:id="n16" target="#a16" n="16"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 226, n. 6</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>entreat</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n17" target="#a17" n="17"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 226, n. 7</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>by</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n18" target="#a18" n="18"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 226, n. 8</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>the service of thy saving</quote>.</note>
      </noteGrp>
